<div id="2026-08-30-git-audit-todos-fixed" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-30 — Git-related Application Error Audit todos closed</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Closed five git-related Application Error Audit todos that were flooding the panel: #2351–#2354 (all `git branch --show-current -> exit=128` benign errors on image-only Docker hosts) and #2307 (`git_merge` schema target issue).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> These todos were generated from the same benign root cause: `git branch --show-current` exits with code 128 on hosts without `.git` metadata (image-only Docker containers). Per the known fixed classes documented in the Application Error Audit system, this error is benign and should be demoted to info-level logging rather than flooding the audit panel. The code at `Comserv/Util/Git.pm:485-497` already maps exit=128+empty-output to `info` level, but the initial scan still created error todos. These duplicates needed closing as documented: "Keep one tracker for prod1 image recreate; close sibling dups as duplicates."</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> Closed todos 2352–2354 and 2307 via `POST /api/todo/update` with status=3 (DONE) and verification comments. Kept #2351 as the canonical tracker (occurrence count now 64,960, consolidating all dups). Updated todo list to reflect completion. Verified via API query that all targeted todos show status=3.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm:485-497</code> (benign exit=128 mapping already existed); audit API endpoints `/api/todo/update` and `/api/todo/done_with_log`</p>
</div>